/-!
# Proof-oriented lean-miniscript modules

This umbrella exports canonical Script codec round trips and preservation of
execution, runtime limits and modeled Tapscript verification, conformance,
structural, inference, surface normalization, generated-satisfaction contracts,
Core/Surface satisfaction and dissatisfaction correctness, stack-growth,
active-path Script resource observations, terminal VERIFY fusion resource
preservation, and runtime prefix-bound guarantees without adding their proof
graph to the stable executable facade. Generated final satisfactions also
expose one concrete resource observation bounded by the jointly selected stack
and dynamic paths, including the context-specific limits certified by sane
fragments. Raw satisfier candidates exist exactly when a valid fragment is
structurally satisfiable under the environment's atom material, and the policy
layer proves its text round trip and that compiled policies preserve the
policy's meaning. PSBT proofs cover exact framing round trips in both
directions, combiner algebra, and finalizer witnesses produced by the existing
descriptor satisfaction and Core verification entry points.
Whole-PSBT finalization and extraction preserve every input's scriptSig and
witness through network serialization under uint64 witness length bounds.
The input-property theorem states separate contracts for retained final
fields and generated verification evidence in each finalization context.
-/
